these\nchoices, the notation for the functor\n<MATH_0005> in Section <REF_0004> and\n<MATH_0006> in Section <REF_0005>\nseems reasonable.\nIn this section we compare our notation with that of SGA4.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0001>Presheaves:<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> Let <MATH_0007> be a functor\nbetween categories.\nThe functor <MATH_0008> is denoted <MATH_0009> in <REF_0006>.\nThe functor <MATH_0010> is denoted <MATH_0011> in <REF_0007>.\nThe functor <MATH_0012> is denoted <MATH_0013> in\n<REF_0008>.\nIn other words, we have\n<MATHSEG_0001>versus<MATHSEG_0002>\nThe reader should be cautioned that different notation is used for these\nfunctors in different parts of SGA4.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0002>Sheaves and continuous functors:<TEXTBFCLOSE_0002>\nSuppose that <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015> are sites and that\n<MATH_0016> is\na continuous functor (Definition <REF_0009>).\nThe functor <MATH_0017> is denoted <MATH_0018> in <REF_0010>.\nThe functor <MATH_0019> is denoted <MATH_0020> in\n<REF_0011>.\nIn other words, we have\n<MATHSEG_0003>versus<MATHSEG_0004>\nWhen <MATH_0021> defines a morphism of sites\n<MATH_0022>\n(Definition <REF_0012>)\nwe see that the associated morphism of topoi\n(Lemma <REF_0013>) is the same as that in\n<REF_0014>.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0003>Sheaves and cocontinuous functors:<TEXTBFCLOSE_0003>\nSuppose that <MATH_0023> and <MATH_0024> are sites and that\n<MATH_0025> is\na cocontinuous functor (Definition <REF_0015>).\nThe functor <MATH_0026> (Lemma <REF_0016>) is denoted <MATH_0027> in\n<REF_0017>.\nThe functor <MATH_0028> is denoted <MATH_0029> in\n<REF_0018>.\nIn other words, we have\n<MATHSEG_0005>versus<MATHSEG_0006>\nThus the morphism of topoi associated to <MATH_0030> in\nLemma <REF_0019>\nis the same as that in <REF_0020>.\n\n<STRUCT_0008><STRUCT_0009>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0004>Morphisms of Topoi:<TEXTBFCLOSE_0004> If <MATH_0031> is a morphism of topoi given\nby the functors <MATH_0032> then the functor <MATH_0033>\nis denoted <MATH_0034> in <REF_0021>.\nWe will use <MATH_0035> to denote pullback of sheaves of sets\nor more generally sheaves of algebraic structure\n(Section <REF_0022>).\nWe will use <MATH_0036> to denote pullback of sheaves of modules\nfor a morphism of ringed topoi\n(Modules on Sites, Definition <REF_0023>).\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2d6baa0a843b7f0ffb4503fa16b185a97f656f2273511fcea8712f6b10e45f60", "unit_id": "tag:0CMZ:prose-0001"}
